{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Therefore say.</b> One must know why it was necessary to say ״לָכֵן״ after saying in the adjacent verse ״תַּחַת אֲשֶׁר קִנֵּא״ — which is also the same import as the statement ״לָכֵן״, so one must necessarily say that it is an expression of oath, as they said, of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah 6:4): ״לָכֵן״ is nothing but an oath, as it is written (I Samuel 3:14): ״לָכֵן נִשְׁבַּעְתִּי לְבֵית עֵלִי״. And one still needs to know why an oath was necessary. And to this one may say that an oath was necessary to reinforce the covenant of peace — for even though his sons may not be worthy of this thing, HaShem will fulfill the oath." "<b>Further,</b> the verse may be explained according to their words, of blessed memory (Zevachim 101b), who said that before the act of Zimri, Pinchas had not been consecrated as a priest, because he was born (already circumcised?) and had not been anointed, and after he performed his act of zealotry the priesthood came to him. Now, in this matter there are two paths: one is the path of forgiveness, and the second is the path of gift. The path of forgiveness is that HaShem would forgive him the penalty that penalized him for not having been anointed at the time of the anointing of the priests; and the path of gift is that He would give him the priesthood anew, in the manner it was given to Aharon, even though his father and his brother were not priests. And according to law there is a difference between whether the matter is by way of forgiveness or by way of gift: by way of forgiveness, no formal act of acquisition is required, whereas by way of gift a formal act of acquisition is required, and as long as they have not acquired from his hand, the recipient does not acquire title to the gift except in that which has already reached him." "<b>Further,</b> in the path of gift there are two disadvantages that do not exist if it were by way of forgiveness. For by way of forgiveness, if He forgives him the penalty and he returns to the priesthood of Aharon, then those who contest his priesthood are also silenced — in the same manner that they were silenced regarding the priesthood of Aharon, from whom he descends — which is not so by way of gift, where the contestants still have grounds against him in the same way they had against Aharon at first, and all the more so since they harbored hatred toward him because of the killing of the prince, etc. Second, by way of gift there is room to say that the matter is an innovation and you have in it nothing but its novelty — which is not so if it were by way of forgiveness and he returns to the priesthood of Aharon, where the matter returns to its root, and his descendants are like him. You thus find that in three respects the path of forgiveness is more fitting than the path of gift: first, that it requires no act of acquisition; second, that one need not worry about contestants; third, that it extends to him and to his descendants after him." "<b>Now,</b> it seemed proper in the eyes of the Master, HaShem, blessed be He, to exalt the merit of Pinchas by making the matter come by way of gift — that he be a priest from his own side and not from the side of the branch that came forth from him, for his glory. And that is what He said: <b>Behold, I give him</b> — by way of gift. And the God of the universe rectified all three things that present difficulty when the matter is by way of gift, as we have said: corresponding to what we said — that a gift requires an act of acquisition — He said ״לָכֵן״, an expression of oath; and corresponding to the concern about contestants, He said <b>Behold, I give him My covenant of peace</b>; and corresponding to the concern that the matter applies only to Pinchas and is merely an innovation, He said <b>and it shall be for him and for his seed after him</b>, etc. — so that this gift is delivered into his hand by oath from the mouth of the Creator, that it shall be his for peace, and for his seed after him, an everlasting priesthood. And I have already drawn your attention in two or three places that the priesthood is a soul so called in the realm of souls, and HaShem promised Pinchas that this holy branch called priesthood would extend through his seed — and this is the sod of His saying ״an everlasting priesthood.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :register {:flags {3 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:27.370696981Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}